uperf-linux-rev source packaging
=================================

The upstream repository keeps Debian metadata in packaging/debian. A release
source tree must copy that directory to top-level debian before running Debian
tools.

Cargo.lock and Rust 1.96 are part of the source contract. debian/rules sets
CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true; populate the Cargo cache with `cargo fetch --locked`
before a local build. A distribution upload should use reviewed vendored
sources or packaged Rust crates instead of granting network access to the
build.

Release codegen intentionally leaves binaries unstripped and Debian builds
retain line-table debug information. `dh_strip` owns final stripping and
generation of matching automatic debug-symbol packages, and therefore also
honours Debian's `DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nostrip` convention. Standalone release
archives should likewise strip only staged copies and retain their matching
debug artifacts instead of stripping Cargo's build output in place.

The JSON files below config/schema are generated release artifacts from the
uperf-core schemars models. Configuration-type changes must regenerate all
three files and include the schema diff in review.
